From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:33:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Hand players over between worlds ticked by different threads

PlayerList.moveToWorld splits in two when the old and new worlds are ticked by
different threads: the player leaves on the old world's thread, stays in the
player list, and arrives on the new world's thread after whatever that thread
had queued; packets sent meanwhile follow it there. A player on the way cannot
be teleported again. A login aimed at a world on its own thread lands in the
main world and is handed over once the login is done, and respawns may go
anywhere. The player-side clock (EntityPlayer.athenaTick) runs on across such a
move. teleportAsync, teleportGradually and preloadChunks may be called from any
thread: the teleport queue stays on the server thread and moves each player on
its own world's thread, and each world thread drains its own preloads. Entities
other than players move only between worlds ticked by the same thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

